# Clanker cleanliness

Clanker cleanliness is of utmost importance. Leftover processes are a defect.

Do not leave test/dev servers, debug binaries, watchers, or other background jobs running after the check that needed them.

If Clanker started it, Clanker stops it when the work is done, or when the Meat Bag stops the task. Prefer a short-lived process over a parked one.

Kill the process Clanker spawned. Do not hunt unrelated long-running services the Meat Bag already had.
